{
  name = "cpp";
  description = "Write, review, or improve modern C++ code. Aligned with the Google C++ Style Guide, with a few house exceptions — `.cpp`/`.hpp` extensions, 100-column lines, `PascalCase` functions (or `snake_case` to match surrounding ROS2-style code), `snake_case_` class members, `kCamelCase` constants, `#ifndef` header guards, only trivial non-template definitions in headers, and `assert()` from `<cassert>` for invariants. Use when building new C++ features, refactoring, or reviewing modern C++17/20/23 code. For ROS2 concerns (executors, callback groups, QoS, intra-process), use the `ros2` skill instead.";
